data: {"text":"1. The Complainant, Mr. Deepak Ranjan, is a 'consumer' within the meaning of Section 2(7) of the Consumer Protection Act, 2019, having"}

data: {"text":" purchased goods for consideration which has been paid or"}

data: {"text":" promised or partly paid and partly promised, or under any system of de"}

data: {"text":"ferred payment for his personal use and not for resale or for"}

data: {"text":" any commercial purpose.\n\n2. The Opposite Party, ElectroMart India Pvt. Ltd., 4th Floor, Cyber Tower, DLF Phase II, Gurugram - 122002 (Through its Authorised Service Centre"}

data: {"text":" at Patna), is engaged in the business of selling electronic goods including televisions, home appliances and related services through"}

data: {"text":" online portals and physical stores across India.\n\n3. On 12.01.2026, the Complainant purchased a Samsung 55-inch QLED Smart TV (Model QA55Q60CAKL"}

data: {"text":"XL) from the Opposite Party's official online portal for a consideration of Rs. 89,990/- vide Invoice No. EM-2026-00045178 dated 12.01.2026. The payment"}

data: {"text":" was made through Credit card transaction via HDFC Bank, ending 4421.\n\n4. The TV was delivered to the Complainant's"}

data: {"text":" residence on 18.01.2026 and was properly installed by the Opposite Party's authorised technician. The installation"}

data: {"text":" was completed without any apparent issues and the TV was functioning normally at the time of installation.\n\n5. Within 22 "}

data: {"text":"days of installation, on 09.02.2026, the display panel started showing vertical lines and the TV would intermittently shut down without any external interference or misuse by"}

data: {"text":" the Complainant. The Complainant immediately raised complaint ticket No. SAM-PAT-114578 on 10.02.2026 through the Opposite Party's customer"}

data: {"text":" service portal.\n\n6. Despite three site visits by the service technician between 12.02.2026 and 28.03.2026, the defect persists and the TV"}

data: {"text":" remains dysfunctional. The Opposite Party has unreasonably refused to replace the unit despite the manufacturing defect being clearly within the warranty period and visible from the very first failure."}

data: {"text":" Multiple follow-up emails dated 02.03.2026, 18.03.2026, and 05.04.2026 sent by the Complainant have gone unanswered,"}

data: {"text":" demonstrating the Opposite Party's callous attitude towards customer grievances.\n\n7. The conduct of the Opposite Party amounts to 'deficiency in service' within"}

data: {"text":" the meaning of Section 2(11) of the Consumer Protection Act, 2019, and the TV supplied constitutes a 'defect' within the meaning"}

data: {"text":" of Section 2(10) of the said Act. The refusal to replace a defective product within warranty"}

data: {"text":" period and ignoring customer complaints constitutes an 'unfair trade practice' within the meaning of Section 2(47) of the Consumer Protection Act, 2019.\n\n8. This Hon"}

data: {"text":"'ble Commission has territorial jurisdiction to entertain the present complaint as the cause of action arose at Patna where"}

data: {"text":" the goods were delivered, installed, and where the deficiency in service manifested. The Opposite Party's authorised service centre is also located at Patna, making it the appropriate forum for adj"}

data: {"text":"udication of the present dispute.\n\n9. This Hon'ble Commission has pecuniary jurisdiction to entertain the present complaint as the total claim amount including"}

data: {"text":" refund of purchase price, compensation for mental agony and harassment, and litigation costs aggregates to Rs. 1,54,990/"}

data: {"text":"-, which falls well within the pecuniary jurisdiction of the District Commission up to Rs. 1 Crore as provided under Section 34(1) of"}

data: {"text":" the Consumer Protection Act, 2019.\n\n10. The present complaint is filed well within the limitation period prescribed under Section 69 of the Consumer Protection Act, 2019. The cause of action arose on 09.02"}

data: {"text":".2026 being the date when the first defect manifested, and continues till date due to the ongoing"}

data: {"text":" deficiency in service by the Opposite Party.\n\n11. The Complainant is entitled to refund of the entire purchase consideration of Rs. 89,990/-"}

data: {"text":" along with reasonable compensation of Rs. 50,000/- for mental agony, harassment, and inconvenience caused due to the defective"}

data: {"text":" product and deficient service. The Complainant is also entitled to litigation costs of Rs. 15,000/- for"}

data: {"text":" being compelled to approach this Hon'ble Commission for redressal of grievances.\n\n12"}

